-- title:
--   Induced trace identities for the quaternionic lift seed
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, together with a group isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, and let $\zeta\in\mathbb{C}$ satisfy $\zeta^4=-1$. Write $Q=\mathtt{quatH}\,e$ for the subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ consisting of the elements $\gamma$ whose image $e(\gamma)$ both lifts to a matrix in the distinguished set `P16` of matrices over $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ (via the reduction `red`) and has determinant $1$, and $C=\mathtt{c4H}\,e$ for the cyclic subgroup generated by $(e^{-1}(\bar t))^2$; let $L^{Q}$ and $L^{C}$ be the corresponding fixed fields. The Hecke eigensystem $\mathtt{liftTraceSeed}\,e\,Q$ over $L^{Q}$ has level $(1)$ and, at a prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{L^{Q}}$, coefficients $a(v)=\operatorname{tr}M_v$ and $b(v)=\det M_v$, where $M_v$ is a chosen matrix over $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ in the monoid generated by `Slift` and `Tlift` reducing to $e(\mathtt{seedFrob}\,Q\,v)$; $\iota=\mathtt{iotaZsqrtdNegTwo}$ is the embedding $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\sqrt{-2}\mapsto\sqrt{2}\,i$, and $\mathtt{artinValue4}\,e\,h\zeta\,\mathfrak{P}$ is the value of the order-dividing-four character $\mathtt{chiGal4}\,e\,h\zeta$ of $C$ at the Frobenius datum $\mathtt{seedFrob}\,C\,\mathfrak{P}$. The assertion is that there is a finite set $S$ of primes of $\mathcal{O}_{L^{Q}}$ such that for every $v\notin S$: first, whenever $\mathfrak{P}_1\neq\mathfrak{P}_2$ are two distinct primes of $\mathcal{O}_{L^{C}}$ lying over $v$, one has $\iota(a(v))=\mathtt{artinValue4}(\mathfrak{P}_1)+\mathtt{artinValue4}(\mathfrak{P}_2)$ and $\iota(b(v))=\mathtt{artinValue4}(\mathfrak{P}_1)\cdot\mathtt{artinValue4}(\mathfrak{P}_2)$; and second, whenever $\mathfrak{P}$ is a prime of $\mathcal{O}_{L^{C}}$ over $v$ with inertia (residue) degree $2$, one has $a(v)=0$ in $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ and $\iota(b(v))=-\mathtt{artinValue4}(\mathfrak{P})$.
--
--   This is the local dictionary, prime by prime outside a finite exceptional set, expressing that over the sextic field fixed by the quaternionic subgroup the lift-trace Hecke system agrees with the two-dimensional representation induced from an order-four character of the cyclic index-two subgroup, in the split and in the inert case respectively; it is the arithmetic input of the octahedral construction of Langlands and Tunnell. It is used in the derivation of the quadratic ray class character table for this eigensystem from the determinant dictionary row.
